  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>pagemldivide</keyword>
  <short_description>Page-wise left matrix division.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>X = pagemldivide(A, B)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[X, rcondA] = pagemldivide(A, B)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>A</param_name>
      <param_description>a single or double N-D array: each page <b>A(:,:,i)</b> is a matrix.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>B</param_name>
      <param_description>a single or double N-D array with as many rows as <b>A</b>.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>X</param_name>
      <param_description>the array of solutions: <b>X(:,:,i) = A(:,:,i) \ B(:,:,i)</b>.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>rcondA</param_name>
      <param_description>a 1-by-1-by-pages array of reciprocal condition estimates of the pages of <b>A</b>.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p><b>X = pagemldivide(A, B)</b> solves <b>A(:,:,i) * X(:,:,i) = B(:,:,i)</b> for every page. Square pages are solved directly and rectangular pages in the least-squares sense, like <b>mldivide</b>.</p>
    <p>Dimensions beyond the second must be equal or 1: a dimension of size 1 is repeated to match the other input.</p>
    <p>No warning is shown for badly conditioned pages: request <b>rcondA</b> to check them. For a rectangular page it is the estimate for its triangular QR factor.</p>
  </description>
